WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.220
QuietRelay helps small community teams plan stock and volunteers.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:13.110
The local Strands agent inspects conflicts, selects a permitted plan, and validates it.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:18.140
Four requests are ready. The rice shortage remains unresolved.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:27.280
Import another queue: seven anonymous requests, six stock lots, and three volunteers. One request needs both rice and milk.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.320
Check all three tables before replacing the current inputs.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:41.180
Loading clears previous decisions. Now run the local agent.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:47.230
Six requests are ready. Expired rice is excluded, leaving one shortage.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:52.240
The allocation shows the original stock and volunteer IDs.

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.390
Approve locally. No volunteer is dispatched and no payment is sent.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:01:01.420
Save, reload, and restore. Both the approval and follow-up decision survive.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:07.560
The handover includes every request. Five still await coordinator review.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.580
A changed input makes this saved plan inconsistent. It is rejected.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:17.610
Editing current inputs clears the old plan and approvals.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.700
A workspace file restores the review. This is a synthetic prototype, without field-impact evidence.
